# Environment Configuration for OctoFit Frontend

## Setup Instructions

### For Local Development (Localhost)

The frontend automatically falls back to `http://localhost:8000/api` when `VITE_CODESPACE_NAME` is not set.

**No additional configuration needed** - just run:
```bash
npm run dev --prefix octofit-tracker/frontend
```

### For GitHub Codespaces

When deploying to GitHub Codespaces, you must set the `VITE_CODESPACE_NAME` environment variable.

#### Option 1: `.env.local` file (Recommended for Development)

1. Create `octofit-tracker/frontend/.env.local`:
```bash
VITE_CODESPACE_NAME=your-codespace-name
```

2. Replace `your-codespace-name` with your actual Codespace name (e.g., `legendary-potato-pjq5wqj5vg46c66jq`)

3. The API will automatically use: `https://your-codespace-name-8000.app.github.dev/api`

#### Option 2: Environment Variable (CI/CD or Shell)

```bash
export VITE_CODESPACE_NAME=your-codespace-name
npm run dev --prefix octofit-tracker/frontend
```

#### Option 3: Build Time

```bash
VITE_CODESPACE_NAME=your-codespace-name npm run build --prefix octofit-tracker/frontend
```

## Finding Your Codespace Name

Your Codespace name appears in:
- The browser URL: `https://your-codespace-name.github.dev`
- The VS Code window title
- Codespaces settings page

## API Endpoint Resolution

The frontend determines the API base URL as follows:

```javascript
const codespaceName = import.meta.env.VITE_CODESPACE_NAME;

if (codespaceName) {
  // Codespaces URL
  baseUrl = `https://${codespaceName}-8000.app.github.dev/api`;
} else {
  // Local development fallback
  baseUrl = 'http://localhost:8000/api';
}
```

## .gitignore

The `.env.local` file is already included in `.gitignore` and will not be committed to the repository.
